#
# Purpose:
#   Compact knowledge file (~20K tokens) targeting qwen3.5:27b (dense,
#   27B active parameters/token, ~17GB at Q4_K_M) for high-quality
#   offline XQL data model rule generation on CPU-only hardware.
#
# Context budget:
#   - System prompt: ~20K tokens
#   - Free for user prompts: ~40-110K tokens (depending on num_ctx)
#   - Total context: 131072 tokens (qwen3.5:27b native max: 256K)
#
# Reference content:
#   Section 7 is a Patterns Catalogue of skeleton meta-examples (one
#   per transformation family) rather than full vendor rules. This
#   keeps the system prompt lean and discourages verbatim copying.
#   Production-validated reference rules live in
#   PRIVATE_DOCS/packs/<vendor>/ in the GoCortex IDE repository.
#
# Extraction pattern families covered (Section 7):
#   A. JSON field extraction (json_extract_scalar)
#   B. Syslog/positional parsing (split + arrayindex on _raw_log)
#   C. Label/value array extraction (regextract on structured arrays)
#   D. Arrow operator on parsed JSON objects (field -> Key.SubKey)
#   + Role-filtered arrays of objects (Section 9.7)
#   + MITRE arraymap with no double-wrap (Section 9.8)
#   + Banded numeric scoring, object-type-gated IP, scalar-from-array
#
# Usage:
#   ollama create gocortex-xql-offline -f ollama_xql_modelfile_offline
#   ollama run gocortex-xql-offline
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
# GoCortexIO
# ================================================================
#
# PARAMETER TUNING NOTES:
#
# num_ctx 131072
#   Half of qwen3.5:27b native 256K context. Provides ~20K for system
#   prompt + ~40-110K for user prompts (sample logs, API specs, conversation).
#   Increase to 262144 if you have 32GB+ RAM and need very large sample sets.
#
# temperature 0.3
#   Low temperature for deterministic, precise XQL output. XQL is a
#   formal language -- creativity is counterproductive. Raise to 0.5
#   only if outputs feel too repetitive across different log types.
#
# num_predict 16384
#   Hard cap on output tokens. A complete 40-field XQL rule with full
#   XDM_CONST if-chains is ~2-3K tokens. 16384 gives 5-8x headroom
#   for thinking + rule output, while preventing infinite loops that
#   previously ran for 17+ hours (8,224+ lines) without producing a
#   rule. Previously set to -1 (unlimited) which allowed the model to
#   spin indefinitely in "Final check" schema enumeration loops.
#   Increase to 32768 only if rules are being truncated mid-output.
#
# repeat_penalty 1.18
#   Qwen3.5 thinking mode is prone to infinite loops. Three patterns
#   observed: (1) restating analysis paragraphs, (2) "One detail:
#   xdm.X / Not available" enumeration, (3) "Final check on xdm.X"
#   schema walk-through. 1.05 was insufficient. 1.15 reduced but did
#   not eliminate loops. 1.18 adds further pressure. Note: the schema
#   walk loops use different field names each line, so repeat_penalty
#   alone cannot fully prevent them -- the num_predict cap and
#   instruction rewrites (see #1 and #6) are the primary defence.
#   If XQL output quality degrades, try 1.15 as a compromise.
#
# THINKING MODE:
#   qwen3.5:27b has thinking mode enabled by default. The model will
#   use <think>...</think> blocks to reason step by step before
#   generating output. This is ideal for XQL rule generation as it
#   lets the model plan field mappings before writing code. No
#   explicit Ollama parameter is needed -- it is a model-native
#   feature. To disable thinking (not recommended), prepend /no_think
#   to your prompt.
#
# WHY SKELETON META-EXAMPLES INSTEAD OF FULL VENDOR RULES:
#   Embedding three or four full vendor rules (Imperva, Cisco WSA,
#   PANW IoT, ExtraHop, GuardDuty) was observed to cause the model to
#   echo vendor-specific field names and structures into unrelated
#   outputs. Section 7 now provides a Patterns Catalogue: one short
#   <vendor_field> / <XDM_FIELD> skeleton per transformation family.
#   This forces the model to generalise from the pattern shape rather
#   than mirror a single template, and it keeps ~120K tokens free for
#   user sample logs and API specs.
#
# ================================================================

