1.4 CORTEX PARSER IDIOMS (READ BEFORE WRITING ANY alter STAGE)

These twelve idioms are non-negotiable. Each was observed rejected by
the live Cortex XSIAM parser in April 2026. Skim them now; the full
worked examples are in Section 11.

  (i)   Arithmetic in alter MUST use functions, never infix.
        DO:    subtract(a, b)   add(a, b)   multiply(a, b)   divide(a, b)
        DO NOT: a - b           a + b       a * b            a / b
        Parser symptom: cascade of generic "parse error" lines.

  (ii)  Inside if() predicates, do NOT compose two null comparisons
        with `and` / `or`. Drop the guard (Cortex propagates null) or
        nest if() calls.
        DO NOT: if(_a != null and _b != null, subtract(_b, _a), null)
        DO:     subtract(_b, _a)
        DO:     if(_a != null, if(_b != null, subtract(_b, _a), null), null)

  (iii) Bareword `= true` / `= false` is illegal on string-typed
        columns. Quote the literal, OR cast with to_boolean().
        DO NOT: if(_external = true, false, true)   // _external is string
        DO:     if(_external = "true", false, true)
        DO:     if(to_boolean(_external) = true, false, true)

  (iv)  to_number() returns float. Integer XDM fields (duration, port,
        bytes, packets, pid) MUST be wrapped in to_integer().
        DO:     xdm.event.duration = to_integer(to_number(_ms))

  (v)   xdm.event.start_time and xdm.event.end_time DO NOT EXIST.
        Fold start/end pairs into xdm.event.duration.
        DO:     xdm.event.duration = to_integer(subtract(
                    to_number(_end_ms), to_number(_start_ms)))

  (vi)  arraymap on an array of objects MUST project ONE scalar per
        call via `"@element" -> field`. Returning the whole struct
        (`"@element"` alone) or binding a struct array to an alter
        target is rejected. Use the per-scalar projection (Section 7
        Pattern D' / Section 9.7).
        DO NOT: _x = arrayindex(arrayfilter(<col> -> [],
                    "@element" -> role = "X"), 0)   // struct bind -- BLOCKED
        DO:     _x_field = arrayindex(arrayfilter(arraymap(<col> -> [],
                    if("@element" -> role = "X",
                       "@element" -> field, null)),
                    "@element" != null), 0)

  (vii) JSON-string columns MUST be cast with `-> []` before any
        array function (arraymap, arrayfilter, arraystring,
        arraydistinct, array_length).
        DO:     arraymap(participants -> [], ...)
        DO NOT: arraymap(participants, ...)

  (viii) Every `_var` you define MUST flow into an xdm.* assignment
        through some intermediary chain. Cortex hard-blocks orphans
        on _gc_raw datasets ("Data Model Rules contains unused fields").

  (ix)  When the parser reports two adjacent errors, the EARLIEST is
        almost always the root cause; the rest are cascade noise from
        the parser losing position. Fix the first defect and recompile.

  (x)   One-sided source/target mirroring. When a vendor delivers a
        SINGLE actor (offender / attacker / principal) and no normalised
        counterparty, mirror that actor's identity into BOTH xdm.source.*
        AND xdm.target.* (Section 9.9). Mirror the explicit pair list:
        ipv4, host.ipv4_addresses, host.hostname, user.username, user.upn,
        is_internal_ip. Note: xdm.{source,target}.is_external does NOT
        exist; the only canonical sink for an external/internal boolean
        is is_internal_ip (invert before assigning).
        DO:     xdm.source.ipv4 = _offender_ip,
                xdm.target.ipv4 = _offender_ip      // mirror

  (xi)  No sibling references inside a single alter stage. Cortex
        evaluates all targets in one alter in PARALLEL, so a target
        cannot read a sibling temp defined in the same stage -- the
        parser reports it as "unknown field <_var>". Cross-temp
        derivations MUST be split across multiple alter stages, with
        later stages referencing only temps from prior stages.
        DO NOT: | alter
                    _offender_ip = if(_obj_type = "ipaddr", _obj_val, null),
                    _offender_ipv4_arr = arraycreate(_offender_ip)
        DO:     | alter
                    _offender_ip = if(_obj_type = "ipaddr", _obj_val, null)
                | alter
                    _offender_ipv4_arr = arraycreate(_offender_ip)

  (xii) concat() / arraystring() bodies do NOT count toward variable
        reach. The validator's reach analyser stops at function
        boundaries and cannot credit a `_var` whose only consumer is
        inside a concat()/arraystring() body -- Cortex reports it as
        "Data Model Rules contains unused fields". Either inline the
        derivation directly into the concat()/arraystring() expression,
        OR drain the temp through a bareword identity assignment first.
        DO NOT: _categories_joined = arraystring(_categories_arr, ", "),
                _description = concat("Cats: ", _categories_joined)
                  // _categories_joined reported orphan
        DO:     _description = concat("Cats: ", arraystring(_categories_arr, ", "))

If any of (i)-(xii) is unclear, stop and re-read Section 11 before
emitting the rule.


